WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.734
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:05.067
You're here.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:06.968
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:10.934
Well, guys, this Sunday is
the 94th Academy Awards.

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:11.934
Yeah.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:13.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.367
That's right, the Oscars are 94,

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:18.300
and typical Hollywood, they're
all dating statues in their 20s.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.100
I can't wait.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.000
The biggest stars
walking the red carpet,

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.434
being asked "Who are you
wearing? Who swabbed you?"

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:26.434
You know.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:27.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:30.167
Quick heads-up, if you hear
a piercing shriek

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.467
halfway through the show,

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.601
that's just me
when Questlove wins the Oscar.

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.367
Meanwhile, Quest, you're
going to enjoy this, all right?

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:46.734
So, the Oscar gift bag this year
has a value of $140,000.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:47.834
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.334
$140,000.

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:50.434
Can we see what's in the bag?

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.133
Oh, it's gas. Oh, fantastic.

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.133
It's a gallon of gas.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:57.067
-Wow.
-A gallon -- a whole gallon.

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.801
The big nominees this year
are "The Power of the Dog,"

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:05.234
"CODA," "Belfast," and a bunch
of others you started streaming

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:06.534
and forgot to finish.

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:07.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.133
But this is new.

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.934
I saw that this year,
there's a Fan Favorite Award

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:13.534
that will be decided
by a vote on Twitter.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.767
That's why the Oscar will go
to a TikTok

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.367
of a guy falling
off a golf cart.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:19.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:20.734
Well, this year, the Oscars
are paying tribute

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:23.501
to "The Godfather"
for its 50th anniversary.

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:24.501
They'll be like -- Yeah.

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:28.834
Yep, they're like,
"We're here to honor

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.267
all the great 'Godfather' movies
--

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.234
'The Godfather,'
'Godfather: Part II.'

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.300
You know, those two movies."

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.434
That's right,
the Oscars will also pay tribute

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:39.968
to the James Bond franchise.

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:42.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:45.934
It makes sense because there are
just so many classic Bond films.

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.300
I mean, here,
check out this promo

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.934
that The Academy just released.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.601
-This year, The Academy
is excited to take a look back

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:54.133
at every James Bond film,
including...

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:12.601
-♪ Blue, da ba dee, da ba die ♪

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:13.634
-...and of course...

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.334
-There you go. Excellent.

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.701
A lot of great classics.
-Wow. Classic.

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:20.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:22.467
-[ Chuckles ]
-Wow.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:25.100
-Speaking of movies,
everyone is talking about this.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.100
The director of "The Batman"
just released a deleted scene

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.334
showing Robert Pattinson
facing off against The Joker.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.501
-Ooh.
-It's pretty shocking.

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.534
I had no idea that you could
release a three-hour movie

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:36.801
and still have deleted scenes.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:37.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:39.334
Impossible.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:40.601
But the scene
is really something.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:42.367
I mean, we haven't seen
a Batman face off

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.200
against The Joker in months.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.367
Some TV news.

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:51.834
Today, the second season
of "Bridgerton"

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.501
started streaming on Netflix.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:54.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:55.934
Oh, yeah.

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.701
Mother's Day came early
this year.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.534
Yeah, that's right.
-Oh, oi.

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:02.367
-At least I -- Apparently,
a lot of the fans were upset

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:05.033
'cause this season
has way fewer sex scenes.

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.601
[ Audience ohs ]
-Oh.

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:08.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:09.567
-I know.

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.267
"Bridgerton"
without the sex scenes,

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.133
which explains this new
Netflix message I saw.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:15.868
-Wow.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:18.667
[ Laughter ]
-Isn't that weird?

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.200
Got even weirder when Netflix
added more sex scenes

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.367
to "Is It Cake?"

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:25.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.033
-Yes!
-Did you guys --

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:29.133
Did you guys see this?

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:31.033
North Korea just released
a hype video

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:33.334
for its most recent
missile launch.

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:34.868
Take a look --
Take a look at this. It's real.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:37.334
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:43.767
♪♪

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:50.200
♪♪

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:53.934
-Wait.
-That's real.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:54.968
-No.
-Yeah.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.534
-Y'all did that.
-No, that's real, man.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.367
That's actually real, yeah.
-No, this is the part where --

00:03:58.367 --> 00:03:59.734
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:00.934
-Yeah, no, yeah.

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:02.267
No, nothing says
that you're in charge

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.467
like pointing at something
in slow motion.

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:15.868
♪♪

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:21.400
♪♪

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.167
[ Laughter continues ]

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:25.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:27.234
♪♪

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:28.767
-Dance.

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:32.434
-At a certain point,
everyone was just like,

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:34.934
"Is your watch broken?
What's going on?"

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:36.501
With everything Putin's doing,

00:04:36.501 --> 00:04:38.067
this is Kim Jong-Un's way
of saying,

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.501
"Hey, I'm nuts, too.
Remember me?

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:43.734
Remember me, guys? Come on."

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:45.434
But on the bright side,
Kim Jong-Un was just nominated

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:46.434
for an Oscar --

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:47.767
Best Dictator Short.

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:49.234
-Oh. Nice.
-Yeah.

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:51.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:52.634
Well, this is nice.

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:55.200
Today, President Biden was
in Poland visiting our troops

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.033
and even stayed for some pizza.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:59.567
But I think the jalapeño slice
caught him by surprise.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:01.133
Watch -- Watch this.

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:09.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:18.968
-Oh.

00:05:18.968 --> 00:05:20.334
-You -- [ Laughs ]

00:05:20.334 --> 00:05:22.400
You know it must have been bad
when during a pandemic,

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.868
Biden is like,
"Let me drink from your cup.

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:24.934
Let me --

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:26.367
I need something to --
Hand it over.

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:28.434
Just -- Just spit it
in my mouth.

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:29.901
Just go -- I really --
I don't --

00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:32.567
Hot, hot, hot."

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:33.934
Yeah, the spice
really got to him.

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.067
And this is real.

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:36.367
He was still feeling it
a little later.

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:37.934
This is a real video.
Check it out.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.067
[ Coughing ]

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:53.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.167
-I love that dude.

00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:00.701
I love how he says "pizza pie."

00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:03.667
I don't even think
Mario and Luigi say that.

00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:05.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:06.934
It was like,
"You know what gives me

00:06:06.934 --> 00:06:08.501
worse heartburn that pizza pie?

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:09.834
Pas-- Pasketti."

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:11.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.234 --> 00:06:15.634
Some business news.

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:20.100
IHOP and Pepsi have teamed up to
create the new maple syrup cola.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.033
Here it is.

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:22.167
Yeah.

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:23.501
[ Audience ohs ]

00:06:23.501 --> 00:06:24.901
Yeah, I'm trying to be healthy,
so I'm going to wait

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:27.100
'til they come out
with a diet maple syrup Pepsi.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:31.000
Yeah, it turns out
the executives at IHOP

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.367
are just as drunk
as the customers.

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:33.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.701 --> 00:06:35.067
And finally, a new study

00:06:35.067 --> 00:06:37.701
found that drinking two
to three cups of coffee a day

00:06:37.701 --> 00:06:40.100
could add years to your life.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:45.033 --> 00:06:48.300
On the flip side, if you want
to take years off of your life,

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.601
try the new maple syrup Pepsi
from IHOP.

00:06:50.601 --> 00:06:51.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:53.734
We have a great show.
Give it up for The Roots.

00:06:53.734 --> 00:06:55.000
Go. Come on.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:59.100
[ Tariq rapping indistinctly ]

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:06.067
♪♪

00:07:06.067 --> 00:07:12.968
♪♪

00:07:12.968 --> 00:07:15.334
-What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:16.534
I'm so excited.

00:07:16.534 --> 00:07:18.567
They are the hosts
of "Desus &amp; Mero,"

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:21.267
which airs Thursday nights
at 11:00 on Showtime.

00:07:21.267 --> 00:07:23.968
Desus and Mero are here tonight.

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:25.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:25.934 --> 00:07:28.767
Funny -- Funny dudes.

00:07:28.767 --> 00:07:30.100
Plus, she's amazing.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.534
She's a Grammy-winning artist

00:07:31.534 --> 00:07:34.467
whose new album "Humble Quest"
is out now.

00:07:34.467 --> 00:07:36.634
Maren Morris is here tonight.
-Oh.

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:38.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:40.067
-It's just out today.
-Oh!

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:42.467
-This -- The album is out today.

00:07:42.467 --> 00:07:43.767
"Humble Quest."

00:07:43.767 --> 00:07:45.234
We're going to talk to Maren,

00:07:45.234 --> 00:07:47.067
and then she's going to perform
for us tonight on the show.

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:49.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:51.601 --> 00:07:52.968
Guys, I'm very excited
about this.

00:07:52.968 --> 00:07:55.601
Next Tuesday, I have a new
children's book coming out

00:07:55.601 --> 00:07:57.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
called...

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.767
This is a goodie.

00:08:02.767 --> 00:08:05.033
-Tear-jerker.
-This is -- Yeah.

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:07.467
"More than Paris
and the Eiffel Tower?

00:08:07.467 --> 00:08:09.501
More than cats
with SUPER cat powers."

00:08:09.501 --> 00:08:11.434
[ Awws, laughter, and applause ]

00:08:11.434 --> 00:08:12.567
Anyway, it's -- Yeah.

00:08:12.567 --> 00:08:14.033
Don't cry yet, Higgins.

00:08:14.033 --> 00:08:16.067
But it is a little bit
of a weeper.

00:08:16.067 --> 00:08:17.033
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:08:17.033 --> 00:08:18.534
-Sweet.
-But, to celebrate,

00:08:18.534 --> 00:08:20.200
all next week,
we're going to be showcasing

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.901
some very talented grandmas
on the show,

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:23.367
from all over the country.

00:08:23.367 --> 00:08:26.033
Musicians, dancers, comedians,
lots more.

00:08:26.033 --> 00:08:27.434
So look for that
every night next week.

00:08:27.434 --> 00:08:28.367
It's going to be fun.

00:08:28.367 --> 00:08:29.434
Nana Week!

00:08:29.434 --> 00:08:31.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:31.033 --> 00:08:31.968
Nana.

